The '''Upper Skylands''' is a section of the [[Skylands]] in the [[First Sea]] that hosts quests for players from Lv. 450 to 625, consisting of two main areas.

==Appearance==
===Upper Skylands Entrance===
The entrance to the Upper Skylands, found in the [[Skylands]], is a medium-sized worn-down temple, surrounded by some grass and trees. This is also where the player will find [[God's Guard]]s and the [[Mole]]. Inside the temple is a large pit filled with clouds, which when destroyed, gives access to the Upper Skylands.

===First Sub-Island===
The First Area is a grassy plateau with some houses and a few [[NPCs]], along with a [[Home Points|Home Point NPC]] and a house with a glowing white door that teleports the player back down to the Upper Skylands Entrance. [[Wysper]], the first boss of the Upper Skylands, can be found Across the main tree root. Going across the suspended tree root will lead the player to the Second Area. 

===Second Sub-Island===
The Second Area can be found across the tree root and is much larger than the First. The quests are given here by the [[Sky Quest Giver 2]]. The area is again separated by the giant tree roots, along with a giant bell in the middle section. To the back of this area is a large temple where the [[Instinct Teacher]] is found. There are breakable walls on the sides, which lead to a secret room with eight chests. The walls can only be destroyed by moves that have [[Destructible Physics]], or the player can just Flash Step into it. 
[[File:Temple secret chests.png|thumb]]
To the left of the temple is a giant open area. Here, the second and final boss of the Upper Skylands spawns, the [[Thunder God]], who spawns every 30 minutes and uses [[Rumble|Lightning]] and [[Pole (1st Form)]].

